  "typecheckAfterFollowUp": true,
  "summary": "I added a \"Lights off\" button below the canvas. Clicking it dims the room to a blue night look, keeps a warm lamp on the clock face so the dial stays readable, and relabels the button \"Lights on\". Clicking again restores the warm lighting. Typecheck passes. I checked the night look in a screenshot only (taken with a temporary auto-click, since removed). The real click and the return to day lighting are untested, and I didn't view a day frame after these changes.\n\n`window.__TASK_STATE__` is `{ lightsOn, pendulumAngleDeg }`. `pendulumAngleDeg` is updated every frame and is signed, positive toward the right.\n\nThe pendulum is now a set of native Aura3D nodes in `src/three-bridge/clock.scene.ts`, not the bridged 2-second clip. The clip's phase couldn't be read back, so the reported angle wouldn't have matched what was drawn. I removed the pendulum and its clip from `recipes/clock.mjs` and re-imported. The swing is still sinusoidal with a 2-second period (±12.6°). Hands and weights are unchanged.\n\nThe three lamps from the bridge and the new face lamp now have runtime ids so the button can retune them."
}